# rack-control Mosquitto ACL. Deployed to /etc/mosquitto/acl.
# This file holds usernames and topics only, no secrets.
#
# Least privilege: anything not granted here is denied. There are no global
# "topic" lines (lines before the first "user" would apply to everyone) and
# no "pattern" lines.
#   read  = may receive messages on the topic (Mosquitto 2.x checks this when
#           it delivers a message, so a subscription to a forbidden topic is
#           accepted but never gets anything)
#   write = may publish to the topic (a denied publish is dropped)
# Topic contract: see the plan's MQTT table / docs.
#
# Containment: only orchestrator can both command a PC shutdown and cut a
# relay. A compromised PC reaches only its own cmd/status; a compromised SBC4
# only receives relay commands and reports relay state.

# --- orchestrator: rackctl on the Slate (the privileged client) ------------
user orchestrator
topic write rack/pc/+/cmd
topic write rack/relay/+/set
topic write rack/ceph/maintenance/set
topic read rack/pc/+/status
topic read rack/relay/+/state
topic read rack/sbc4/status
topic read rack/ceph/maintenance/state

# --- sbc4: relay-mqtt sidecar on the Phidget SBC4 ---------------------------
user sbc4
topic read rack/relay/+/set
topic write rack/relay/+/state
topic write rack/sbc4/status

# --- PCs: pc-agent on each Proxmox node (only its own two topics) ----------
user intel-91c45d
topic read rack/pc/intel-91c45d/cmd
topic write rack/pc/intel-91c45d/status

user intel-d1babf
topic read rack/pc/intel-d1babf/cmd
topic write rack/pc/intel-d1babf/status

user intel-177e78
topic read rack/pc/intel-177e78/cmd
topic write rack/pc/intel-177e78/status

user intel-a163f8
topic read rack/pc/intel-a163f8/cmd
topic write rack/pc/intel-a163f8/status

# intel-1ecbc8 is also the Ceph maintenance node (noout/norebalance).
user intel-1ecbc8
topic read rack/pc/intel-1ecbc8/cmd
topic write rack/pc/intel-1ecbc8/status
topic read rack/ceph/maintenance/set
topic write rack/ceph/maintenance/state

# --- switch: NOT an MQTT client in v1 (documentation only) -----------------
# If the switch ever joins as a read-only dashboard, uncomment this block, add
# "switch" to rackpki's user list, and issue it a cert and password. It must
# never get write access.
# user switch
# topic read rack/pc/+/status
# topic read rack/relay/+/state
# topic read rack/sbc4/status
# topic read rack/ceph/maintenance/state
